<!--
  SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
  SEO, Open Graph, Twitter Card and schema.org metadata for a2a-rust docs.

  Notes on choices:
  - The canonical link, og:url, twitter:url, the og/twitter titles and the
    description are site-wide seeds here. scripts/seo_postprocess.py rewrites
    them per page in the built HTML, before deploy (docs.yml), because
    mdBook's Handlebars has no string helpers to derive a page URL. Until
    2026-09-25 a script in the page did this after load, which left every
    served page declaring the site root as its canonical, the cause of
    Search Console's "Duplicate without user-selected canonical"; Google
    advises against changing a canonical with JavaScript.
  - Twitter card is `summary_large_image` so cards render with the full
    preview image on X/Twitter, LinkedIn, Slack, and Discord.
  - JSON-LD describes the project as a whole and legitimately uses the site
    root as its `url`, so it is NOT rewritten per-page.
  - `robots` meta includes `max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large,
    max-video-preview:-1` to permit full descriptions and large preview
    cards in SERPs.
-->

<meta name="description" id="a2a-desc" content="a2a-rust: Rust SDK for the Agent2Agent (A2A) protocol, built to the final v1.0.0 spec. Build interoperable AI agents with type-safe, async Rust.">
<meta name="keywords" content="A2A, Agent2Agent, Agent-to-Agent, Rust, SDK, protocol, AI agents, interoperability, async, tokio, crates.io, multi-agent, agentic, LLM, gRPC, JSON-RPC, REST, SSE, WebSocket">
<meta name="author" content="Tom F.">
<meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-snippet:-1,max-image-preview:large,max-video-preview:-1">
<meta name="googlebot" content="index,follow">

<!-- Apple touch icon (the standard favicon.svg / favicon.png come from the mdBook theme) -->
<link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="/apple-touch-icon.png">

